{"author":{"id":"8d2e0405f08ac6c481f912544d6d5c0f58b2dc14a7e51ad4d499ee7a34567943"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1795083642,"nonce":"op7TegYY+S56DccBGeWKvSTBlqA=","title":"Unit.parse rejects a unit with two slashes, such as W/m/K","message":"`Unit.parse(\"W/m/K\")` raises `ValueError: Cannot parse unit factor 'm/K'`: the grammar splits once on `/` into numerator and denominator. `W/m K` and `W m^-1 K^-1` parse. A thermal conductivity is commonly written W/m/K, so either accept repeated `/` (left to right, each further factor in the denominator) or say in the error which spellings work.","files":null}]}